Description: Run session saves one at a time.
 A save captures the session state when it is requested and writes it only after the drafts it saves are written.
 Saves run at the same time, so a save writing a large draft finishes after a later one, which has no draft left to
 write, and writes its older state over the newer one, which a crash then restores. Text Editor writes a draft at a
 few megabytes a second, so a large draft keeps a save busy for seconds. Saves now run one at a time, in the order they
 are requested, each with the state from when it was requested. A waiting auto-save is replaced by a newer one, and
 saves still waiting when a save for shutdown finishes are completed without running, since Text Editor quits then.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-05
